-- title:
--   Bertini for the double-point quartics
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be uncountable algebraically closed of characteristic zero, $g:X\to\operatorname{Spec}K$, and $s$ sections indexed by $\operatorname{Option}\sigma$ defining a closed immersion, with `centeredOpen s` integral, compact, smooth of relative dimension 2 over $K$. Let $e$ be an equivalence from $\operatorname{Option}(\operatorname{Fin}n)$ to `QuarticIndex σ`. For every nonzero $P$ there is $v$ with $P(v)\neq0$ such that on the centered open $V$, the hyperplane section for the morphism defined by the restricted quartics has integral subscheme, smooth over $K$, and is locally generated by a regular element equal to the coefficient of the combination.
--
--   **Notation.** The iso-open of $s$ (`SectionOpens.isoOpen s`) is the union of the opens on which the morphism $s$ restricts to an isomorphism. `sectionsMorphism k s hs` is the morphism from $X$ to $\operatorname{Proj}$ of the graded polynomial ring in variables indexed by the sections, defined by sections whose iso-opens cover $X$, with $k$ the ring map from the base into $\Gamma(X,\top)$. `centeredOpen s` is the union of the iso-opens of $s_{\mathrm{some}\,i}$. `QuarticIndex σ` is $\sigma\times\sigma\times\operatorname{Option}\sigma\times\operatorname{Option}\sigma$; `doublePointQuartics` are the corresponding degree-4 mixed products of the sections.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement is verbatim from OpenAI's Lean development, with `Definitions` files of this development imported in place of the upstream modules; these are supporting code for the statement.
-- source:
--   OpenAI, Maximal Seshadri constants on arbitrary polarized surfaces, September 23, 2026, https://github.com/openai/math (paper: preprints/Maximal-Seshadri-Constants-on-Arbitrary-Polarized-Surfaces-September-23-2026/main.pdf; Lean: lean/OAI/AlgebraicGeometry/Seshadri, Apache License 2.0); Lean declaration `OAI.MaximalSeshadri.Projective.doublePointQuartics_bertini`, https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/AlgebraicGeometry/Seshadri/Projective/QuarticBertini.lean#L22

